ect runs multiple commands sequentially (version, config, declaration list + N shows, status) — with 30s total context and per-command 30s timeout... Each command gets `context.WithTimeout(ctx, c.timeout)` where ctx is the app's 30s-limited parent. So overall bounded. Fine.\\n\\n18. **`newCLICollector` unexported wrapper** — check if used only in tests. grep.\\n\\n19. **`handlePage` renders full page for non-HTMX**; fine.\\n\\n20. **`runParam`**: if multiple values (len>1) returns errMissingRun? `if !present || len(values)==0 || (len(values)==1 && values[0]==\\\"\\\")` → missing; else bad. len 2 with non-empty → errBadRun. ok.\\n\\n21. **security**: `/fragments/fleet` with instance param calls selectInstance — GET mutating selection; fine for read-only.\\n\\n22. **templates**: check templates and static quickly. Also tests coverage: server_test, app_test etc. Check whether `follow` path and `discoveryLoop` are tested.\\n\\n23. **README says HTMX 2.0.9 vendored** — check static dir.\\n\\n24. **model.go TriggerData.Stale comment** etc fine.\\n\\nPotential findings (need concrete evidence + not style):\\n\\nA. main.go:37-40 — default canopy.json decode error silently ignored; app starts with zero instances and no diagnostics, contradicting inventory.go's stated rejection policy. Required: surface the load error (log.Fatalf or log warning). Strong.\\n\\nB. README.md inventory/HTTP sections omit auto-discovery behavior shipped in discovery.go/main.go (background merge, systemd scanning) — stale doc contradiction. Concrete README lines. Also README says \\\"Canopy treats every Forest as an external service\\\" — fine. The finding: README \\\"Inventory\\\" documents only explicit config, but main.go:60-64 and app.go:111-127 auto-discover and merge instances not present in inventory; operators reading README can't predict fleet contents. Required: document discovery. Good finding.\\n\\nC. collector.go Logs follow parameter dead in production — server.go:~119 passes false always; the follow loop (collector.go:~215-230) is unreachable in shipped behavior and likely untested... check tests first.\\n\\nD. discovery.go:~60 `strings.Contains(workDir, \\\"/misty-step/\\\")` — substring boundary check: a workdir at `/home/u/misty-step` (no trailing slash, exact end) fails; also any repo path containing \\\"/misty-step/\\\" anywhere (e.g. `/srv/misty-step-archive/x`) passes. Weak boundary. Also hardcoded product-specific constant in generic operator view. Hmm — but repo conventions: this is Misty Step's tool, so specific is fine. The substring issue though: workDir `/home/phaedrus/development/misty-step/canopy` contains it, fine. Edge case. Maybe weak; but \\\"contains\\\" vs proper path-prefix is a real correctness nit. Medium.\\n\\nE. discovery.go sanitizeID collision: two sibling dirs `agent_test` and `agent-test` both → id \\\"agent-test\\\"; DiscoverLocalInstances returns both (keyed by root), syncDiscoveredInstances discMap keeps one, other silently dropped with no error. Evidence: discovery.go:185-200 (sanitizeID) + discovery.go:38-44 (map keyed by root, IDs unverified for uniqueness). Required: dedupe by ID or make IDs unique. Medium.\\n\\nF. app.go discoveryLoop hardcoded 5s ticker ignoring inventory intervals; every 5s spawns systemctl — complecting/perf nit. Possibly style.\\n\\nG. server.go handleFleet sets selection without HX-Trigger-After-Swap unlike handleInstance (server.go:47-49 vs 74-77) — is that a bug? handleFleet renders full pageView including fleet; the trigger event \\\"canopy-selection\\\" is used by frontend JS to pause polling? Let me check static JS.\\n\\nLet me check static/main.js and templates to verify G, and tests for follow.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_161dae6d9b704907a9e74b0a","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"ls static templates && grep -n \"canopy-selection\\|follow\" -r static templates server.go collector.go server_test.go collector_test.go | head -40"}},{"t