its handleInstance. So fine.\\n\\nsanitizeLogText: patterns — keyPattern `keys/` prefix etc. Could miss many secret shapes, but redaction best-effort; README warns about sensitive output. Not a concrete defect.\\n\\nNow the invalid-instance edge in discovery: discovered instances bypass `validateListen`? No, validateInstance is applied (discovery.go:33-35).\\n\\nAnother: main.go — when `--config` given, no discovery merge issue; fine.\\n\\nAlso collector.go Collect: `runJSON(ctx, instance, \\\"version\\\", ...)` — exit 6 → VersionData{BuildSHA:\\\"unsupported\\\"}; ok.\\n\\nNow, potential finding: `refreshInterval` stale window `3*a.refreshInterval(instance.ID)` in pageView — maxAge depends on currently-selected; when an instance is selected its stale window shrinks to 6s (3×2s). A selected instance that takes >6s to collect (e.g., slow SSH) flips to \\\"stale\\\" even when healthy. Hmm — is that wrong state? classifyFreshness marks Stale if now >= LastSuccess + maxAge. With selected interval 2s, window 6s; a collect cycle taking 8s (timeout up to 30s) leaves LastSuccess 8s old → rendered \\\"stale\\\" with no Err. Actually state.Err is nil if last attempt succeeded... wait, if a refresh is in progress, Err is nil, LastSuccess is old → stale. So a slow-collecting selected instance will show stale/bad dot while perfectly healthy. Is that a genuine defect? The design comment says \\\"maxAge is the missed-refresh window after which a silent worker is stale.\\\" 3× the interval is a reasonable heuristic, but with per-command timeouts up to 30s, a healthy selected instance whose collection takes >6s is misreported stale every time. Concrete: view.go:151 (pageView passes 3*a.refreshInterval) and collector.go timeout 30s. This is a real behavior bug candidate. Evidence-based: selected interval 2s default → 6s staleness window, but a single Collect can legitimately take longer (6 subprocess calls; each up to 30s). So the UI shows \\\"stale\\\" for healthy instances. Required: base maxAge on observed collect duration or bound it below timeout. I think this is a good finding.\\n\\nAlso verify triggerStatus/StateKnown for audit — skip.\\n\\nLet me collect exact line numbers.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_5d87f2f4e32641ae9cb01f7a","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"discoveryLoop\\|5 \\* time.Second\\|discMap\\|func sanitizeID\\|func DiscoverLocalInstances\\|candidates :=\\|/misty-step/\\|3\\*a.refreshInterval\\|3 \\* a.refreshInterval\" app.go discovery.go view.go; grep -n \"maxAge\\|classifyFreshness\" view.go view_test 2>/dev/null; grep -n \"refreshTimeout\\|defaultCollectorTimeout\" app.go collector.go main.go"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_0607f58156b2460db4078b6f","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"sed -n 145,155p view.go; echo ---; sed -n 180,200p discovery.go; echo ---; sed -n 225,240p app.go"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":1675,"output":1303,"cacheRead":27968,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1144,"totalTokens":30946,"cost":{"input":0.000125625,"output":0.00032575,"cacheRead":0.00041951999999999994,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0008708949999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788550667227,"responseId":"gen-1788550667-LBw5EAULT2FLIcgTJUGi","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_5d87f2f4e32641ae9cb01f7a","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"app.go:105:\t\tgo a.discoveryLoop(ctx)\napp.go:108:func (a *App) discoveryLoop(ctx context.Context) {\napp.go:109:\tticker := time.NewTicker(5 * time.Second)\napp.go:239:\tdiscMap := make(map[string]Instance, len(discovered))\napp.go:241:\t\tdiscMap[disc.ID] = disc\napp.go:250:\t\t\tif updated, stillPresent := discMap[existing.ID]; stillPresent {\ndiscovery.go:15:func DiscoverLocalInstances(ctx context.Context) ([]Instance, error) {\ndiscovery.go:16:\tcandidates := make(map[string]Instance) // keyed by normalized root path\ndisc