ated_at\": \"2026-09-04T18:09:57.811Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": false,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": true,\n      \"live\": true,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-expand-checkout-discovery\",\n    \"title\": \"Discover managed repositories with forest.yaml without requiring pre-existing .forest directory\",\n    \"spec\": \"Enhance DiscoverLocalInstances in discovery.go to detect checkouts declaring forest.yaml and resolve executable forest binaries from PATH or factory root when repo-local ./forest binary is uncompiled.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": \"ca9e23795abebbe11ec519332a79b9c1d96d9ae2\",\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T18:25:46.29Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:02:10.586Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"done: ca9e23795abebbe11ec519332a79b9c1d96d9ae2\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-03T22:01:07.373Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-03T22:01:07.373Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"Enhance DiscoverLocalInstances in discovery.go to detect checkouts declaring forest.yaml and resolve executable forest binaries from PATH or factory root when repo-local ./forest binary is uncompiled.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-03T22:01:07.373Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:02:10.586Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": true,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": false,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-tab-visibility-polling\",\n    \"title\": \"Pause background HTMX polling when browser tab is inactive\",\n    \"spec\": \"Add page visibility detection to pause 2s/10s HTMX polling triggers when document.hidden is true, eliminating unnecessary process execution cycles on background tabs.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": \"0f61b4007878a9bd93ad014a750221fbcb5aff62\",\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T18:34:36.733Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T18:45:58.83Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"done: 0f61b4007878a9bd93ad014a750221fbcb5aff62\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-03T22:01:07.568Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-03T22:01:07.568Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"Add page visibility detection to pause 2s/10s HTMX polling triggers when document.hidden is true, eliminating unnecessary process execution cycles on background tabs.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-03T22:01:07.568Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T18:45:58.83Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": true,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": false,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-log-drawer-experience\",\n    \"title\": \"Replace inline table log expansion with an accessible slide-over drawer\",\n    \"spec\": \"Redesign the Run log viewer to open into an accessible slide-over drawer or modal panel with fixed gutter, clean typography, and a copy button instead of expanding inline within table rows.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": {\n      \"agent\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n      \"principal\": \"none\",\n      \"until\": \"2026-09-04T22:43:58.818Z\"\n    },\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T18:43:58.818Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-03T22:01:07.744Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-03T22:01:07.744Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"Redesign the Run log viewer to open into an accessible slide-over drawer or modal panel with fixed gutter, clean typography, and a copy button instead of expanding inline within table rows.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-03T22:01:07.744Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T18:43:58.818Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": false,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": true,\n      \"live\": true,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"if-critic-silent-canopy-config\",\n    \"title\": \"Malformed default canopy.json is silently ignored at startup\",\n    \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nWhen `-config` is absent and a regular `canopy.json` exists, `main` discards every `LoadInventory` error and continues with an empty inventory. Explicit operator configuration can therefore silently become zero-config discovery. The explicit `-config` path already fails loudly.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\n- If default `canopy.json` is absent, preserve zero-config discovery.\\n- If default `canopy.json` exists as a regular file, load it through `LoadInventory`; any read, decode, trailing JSON, unknown-field, or validation error must terminate startup through the same `load inventory:` boundary as explicit `-config`.\\n- Keep explicit `-config` behavior unchanged.\\n- Align the README precedence statement in `canopy-docs-discovery-alignment` with the corrected behavior before that documentation is completed.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nRun the actual Canopy process from a temporary directory with malformed `canopy.json`, no `-config`, and a safe ephemeral listen address. It exits nonzero, stderr contains `load inventory:`, and no server starts. A companion run with no file starts zero-config and returns 200 from `/healthz`. Existing inventory tests pass.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": {\n      \"agent\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n      \"principal\": \"none\",\n      \"until\": \"2026-09-04T23:08:57.104Z\"\n    },\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T18:54:31.392Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/iron-forest @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: worktree 1788548005453810023-critic, unknown (no forest binary in worktree; forest version unavailable)\\nObserved: main.go:37-41 — when -config is absent, a malformed canopy.json (decode or validation error from LoadInventory) is silently discarded and Canopy starts with zero instances and defaults; no error is logged or surfaced. This contradicts the stated rejection policy at inventory.go:16-17 (\\\"Unknown fields are rejected so a misspelled operational setting cannot silently select a default\\\") and the loud log.Fatalf behavior of the -config path at main.go:31-33.\\nRequired: a default canopy.json that fails to load must fail loudly (or be surfaced to the operator), matching the -config path behavior.\\nProposed spec direction: treat an existing but unparseable default canopy.json as a fatal startup error, identical to -config; keep the true zero-config (no file) path unchanged.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:08:57.104Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:04:07.457Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:04:07.457Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nWhen `-config` is absent and a regular `canopy.json` exists, `main` discards every `LoadInventory` error and continues with an empty inventory. Explicit operator configuration can therefore silently become zero-config discovery. The explicit `-config` path already fails loudly.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\n- If default `canopy.json` is absent, preserve zero-config discovery.\\n- If default `canopy.json` exists as a regular file, load it through `LoadInventory`; any read, decode, trailing JSON, unknown-field, or validation error must terminate startup through the same `load inventory:` boundary as explicit `-config`.\\n- Keep explicit `-config` behavior unchanged.\\n- Align the README precedence statement in `canopy-docs-discovery-alignment` with the corrected behavior before that documentation is completed.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nRun the actual Canopy process from a temporary directory with malformed `canopy.json`, no `-config`, and a safe ephemeral listen address. It exits nonzero, stderr contains `load inventory:`, and no server starts. A companion run with no file starts zero-config and returns 200 from `/healthz`. Existing inventory tests pass.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T18:54:31.226Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:08:57.104Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": false,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": true,\n      \"live\": true,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"if-critic-dead-collector-surface\",\n    \"title\": \"Unused collector and app surface: CommandRunnerFunc, newCLICollector, inventoryCopy, LogView.Complete\",\n    \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nCanopy retains unused adapters/helpers and an uncallable client-side log-follow mode. Production `/logs` is one-shot; every caller passes `follow=false`. These surfaces increase interface and cancellation complexity without serving a shipped behavior.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\nAfter `canopy-log-drawer-experience` completes, confirm the drawer does not require client-side follow mode or `Complete`, then:\\n\\n- Delete unused `CommandRunnerFunc`, `newCLICollector`, and `App.inventoryCopy`.\\n- Change `Collector.Logs` and all implementations/callers/test doubles to the one-shot `Logs(ctx, instance, runID)` contract.\\n- Delete the 100ms follow loop and its timer/cancellation branch.\\n- Delete `LogView.Complete` and its assignment because no template renders it.\\n- Delete any `LogResult.Complete` client use that becomes dead; keep the JSON field only if the documented forest.cli.v2 wire model still requires it.\\n- Preserve retained, evicted, unknown, and failed `/logs` behavior.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nAll Collector implementations and callers compile with the one-shot interface. Focused collector and HTTP handler tests prove exactly one `run logs` command and unchanged retained/evicted/unknown/error output. Structural search finds no removed helper, `follow=true`, or unread `LogView.Complete` surface.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [\n      \"canopy-log-drawer-experience\"\n    ],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T18:54:49.934Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/iron-forest @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: worktree 1788548005453810023-critic, unknown (no forest binary in worktree; forest version unavailable)\\nObserved: dead code with zero references, including in tests — collector.go:38-42 (CommandRunnerFunc adapter), collector.go:68-71 (newCLICollector, returns a private type and is called nowhere), app.go:308-313 (App.inventoryCopy, called nowhere), view.go:138 (LogView.Complete is populated at server.go:136 but rendered by no template; log.html uses only RunID/State/Retained/Exit/Text).\\nRequired: shipped surface should be used or removed; unused exported/typed surface is dead weight per repository conventions (read-only pane, minimal stdlib surface).\\nProposed spec direction: delete CommandRunnerFunc, newCLICollector, and inventoryCopy, and drop LogView.Complete from the view struct (or render it if the log drawer job needs it); no behavior change intended.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:04:07.704Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:04:07.704Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nCanopy retains unused adapters/helpers and an uncallable client-side log-follow mode. Production `/logs` is one-shot; every caller passes `follow=false`. These surfaces increase interface and cancellation complexity without serving a shipped behavior.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\nAfter `canopy-log-drawer-experience` completes, confirm the drawer does not require client-side follow mode or `Complete`, then:\\n\\n- Delete unused `CommandRunnerFunc`, `newCLICollector`, and `App.inventoryCopy`.\\n- Change `Collector.Logs` and all implementations/callers/test doubles to the one-shot `Logs(ctx, instance, runID)` contract.\\n- Delete the 100ms follow loop and its timer/cancellation branch.\\n- Delete `LogView.Complete` and its assignment because no template renders it.\\n- Delete any `LogResult.Complete` client use that becomes dead; keep the JSON field only if the documented forest.cli.v2 wire model still requires it.\\n- Preserve retained, evicted, unknown, and failed `/logs` behavior.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nAll Collector implementations and callers compile with the one-shot interface. Focused collector and HTTP handler tests prove exactly one `run logs` command and unchanged retained/evicted/unknown/error output. Structural search finds no removed helper, `follow=true`, or unread `LogView.Complete` surface.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T18:54:49.748Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:04:07.704Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": false,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": true,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"if-critic-log-sanitize-untested\",\n    \"title\": \"Log redaction (sanitizeLogText) has no regression tests\",\n    \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nCanopy renders retained Run logs after `sanitizeLogText`, but no test defends this server-side credential boundary. The open log drawer adds a copy surface over the same fragment.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\n- Preserve benign and empty log text unchanged.\\n- Redact every currently supported credential form: `keys/`, `key_id=`/`key-id:`, `token=`/`token:`, `Bearer `, `api_key=`/`api-key:`, and standalone `sk-` tokens.\\n- Preserve the non-secret prefix where the current contract does so and replace secret material with `[REDACTED]`.\\n- Cover repeated and multiline matches and the current short-token non-match boundary.\\n- Prove `/logs` sanitizes retained text before HTML rendering; raw secret material must not appear in the response.\\n- Do not expand or redesign redaction policy in this job.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nTable-driven `sanitizeLogText` behavior tests cover each supported form, benign/empty text, repeated/multiline text, and short non-matches. A retained-log handler test asserts `[REDACTED]` is rendered and raw input is absent. Run the focused Go tests and verify the active log drawer still consumes only sanitized `LogView.Text` before approval.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": {\n      \"agent\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n      \"principal\": \"none\",\n      \"until\": \"2026-09-04T23:13:59.043Z\"\n    },\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T18:55:20.281Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/iron-forest @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: worktree 1788548005453810023-critic, unknown (no forest binary in worktree; forest version unavailable)\\nObserved: server.go:211-216 (sanitizeLogText) plus its two regexes at server.go:207-208 have zero test coverage — no *_test.go file references sanitizeLogText or REDACTED (verified by grep). README.md:7 and 26 state Run logs can contain sensitive repository output and must stay protected; the live-integration record on job canopy-operational-multi-repo (2026-09-02T20:10:21Z note) observed credential-linked provider output in a retained Run log. This is an observable safety behavior with no regression test where the repository convention (go test ./... gate in forest.yaml:12-15) expects coverage.\\nRequired: the redaction patterns must have deterministic unit tests proving keys/tokens/bearer strings are redacted and that benign text passes through unchanged.\\nProposed spec direction: add table-driven tests for sanitizeLogText covering each pattern branch (keys/, key_id=, token=, bearer, api_key=, sk- prefixed bearer), short-token non-matches, and multi-line logs, before or alongside the open log drawer redesign.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:13:59.043Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:04:07.474Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:04:07.474Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nCanopy renders retained Run logs after `sanitizeLogText`, but no test defends this server-side credential boundary. The open log drawer adds a copy surface over the same fragment.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\n- Preserve benign and empty log text unchanged.\\n- Redact every currently supported credential form: `keys/`, `key_id=`/`key-id:`, `token=`/`token:`, `Bearer `, `api_key=`/`api-key:`, and standalone `sk-` tokens.\\n- Preserve the non-secret prefix where the current contract does so and replace secret material with `[REDACTED]`.\\n- Cover repeated and multiline matches and the current short-token non-match boundary.\\n- Prove `/logs` sanitizes retained text before HTML rendering; raw secret material must not appear in the response.\\n- Do not expand or redesign redaction policy in this job.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nTable-driven `sanitizeLogText` behavior tests cover each supported form, benign/empty text, repeated/multiline text, and short non-matches. A retained-log handler test asserts `[REDACTED]` is rendered and raw input is absent. Run the focused Go tests and verify the active log drawer still consumes only sanitized `LogView.Text` before approval.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T18:55:20.108Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:13:59.043Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": false,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": true,\n      \"live\": true,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"if-critic-logs-follow-unreachable\",\n    \"title\": \"Logs follow-polling path is unreachable in production and untested\",\n    \"spec\": \"\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": true,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T18:55:44.144Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/iron-forest @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: worktree 1788548005453810023-critic, unknown (no forest binary in worktree; forest version unavailable)\\nObserved: collector.go:231 defines Logs(ctx, instance, runID, follow bool), and collector.go:250-263 implements a 100ms follow-polling loop gated by \\\"if !follow || result.Complete\\\" at collector.go:256. The only production caller, server.go:133, always passes follow=false, so the loop (including its context-cancellation branch) can never execute; no test passes follow=true either (grep over *_test.go shows only follow=false calls at collector_test.go:182,197). The follow code path is therefore both dead weight and an untested hotspot for an observable failure path (ctx cancellation mid-poll).\\nRequired: either the follow path is removed/reserved with a stated reason, or it has a regression test.\\nProposed spec direction: decide the contract for Collector.Logs follow mode: if a live-log follower is planned (README HTTP surface currently documents none), spec it and test the poll-until-complete and ctx-cancel paths; otherwise delete the loop and the follow parameter from the interface in model.go:129.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:04:07.493Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/powder\",\n        \"text\": \"Groomed into if-critic-dead-collector-surface: the follow=true branch and dead helpers are one post-drawer interface cleanup. That item is blocked by canopy-log-drawer-experience so the active drawer can decide whether Complete/follow has a real consumer.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:04:07.673Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/powder\",\n        \"text\": \"abandoned\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_at\": null,\n    \"promotions\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T18:55:43.97Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:04:07.673Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": true,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": false,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-tester-log-secret-redaction\",\n    \"title\": \"Retained Run log rendering and secret redaction lack regression cover\",\n    \"spec\": \"\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": true,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T18:58:26.915Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/iron-forest @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: canopy a101e023933a247460f9828b7cb8d3fce3a681ac\\nSurface: server.go:135 (handleLogs), server.go:211 (sanitizeLogText), route GET /logs. Behaviors: when an operator opens a retained Run log, the response must render the log contents inside \\u003cpre\\u003e while redacting sensitive tokens matching keyPattern and bearerPattern (e.g. sk-*, api_key:*, bearer *) with [REDACTED]; raw secrets must never appear in the rendered HTML fragment. Failing example: invoke GET /logs?instance=one\\u0026run=run-secret with a collector returning a retained log containing \\\"error: sk-ant-api03-1234567890abcdef123456\\\"; today no test exercises GET /logs with retained content or asserts credential redaction. Acceptance: a Builder adds a regression test in server_test.go asserting that GET /logs for a retained log containing sk-* and api_key:* patterns returns HTTP 200, renders state \\\"retained\\\", replaces credential tokens with [REDACTED], and does not include the raw credentials in the response body. Observed: server_test.go covers evicted (Retained: false) and unknown/malformed run IDs only; grep reveals zero tests for sanitizeLogText or retained log rendering. Required: an HTTP regression test in server_test.go for retained log rendering and secret redaction. Proposed test-work: add a server test verifying that GET /logs renders retained run logs and redacts sensitive credential patterns.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:04:07.47Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/powder\",\n        \"text\": \"Duplicate of if-critic-log-sanitize-untested. The surviving item covers helper-level pattern branches plus the retained /logs rendering boundary and relation to canopy-log-drawer-experience.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:04:07.661Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/powder\",\n        \"text\": \"abandoned\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_at\": null,\n    \"promotions\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T18:58:21.936Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:04:07.661Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": true,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": false,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-tester-empty-inventory-rendering\",\n    \"title\": \"Zero-instance empty inventory page and fragment rendering lack regression cover\",\n    \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nCanopy supports a runtime with no configured or discovered instances, but its page and fragment routes are only tested with one configured instance. The empty operator surface can regress to a panic, 500, or broken template unnoticed.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\nWith `NewApp(Inventory{Instances: []}, ...)` and real templates:\\n\\n- `GET /` returns 200 and renders the fleet and selected-instance empty states.\\n- `GET /fragments/fleet` returns 200 and renders `No instances configured.`\\n- `GET /fragments/instance` returns 200 and renders `No instance selected` plus the instruction to add an instance.\\n- No route starts discovery, dereferences a missing selection, or requires host-specific Forest state.\\n\\nThis is test-only work; do not change empty-inventory behavior unless the scenario exposes a real defect.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nA table-driven HTTP test exercises all three routes with the actual embedded templates and an empty in-memory inventory, asserting status 200 and route-specific empty-state text. The focused server tests pass without systemd, Forest binaries, or network fixtures.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": {\n      \"agent\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n      \"principal\": \"none\",\n      \"until\": \"2026-09-04T23:19:02.012Z\"\n    },\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T18:58:37.391Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/iron-forest @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: canopy a101e023933a247460f9828b7cb8d3fce3a681ac\\nSurface: server.go:49 (handlePage), server.go:82 (handleInstance), templates/fleet.html:36, templates/instance.html:145. Behaviors: when Canopy runs with zero configured or discovered instances, GET /, GET /fragments/fleet, and GET /fragments/instance must return HTTP 200 and gracefully render the empty-state templates (\\\"No instances configured.\\\", \\\"No instance selected\\\", \\\"Add an instance to the inventory to begin observing it.\\\") without panic, nil pointer dereference, or HTTP 500. Failing example: initialize NewApp with Inventory{Instances: []} and issue GET /, GET /fragments/fleet, and GET /fragments/instance; today all tests in server_test.go initialize testInventory() with one pre-configured instance, leaving the zero-instance empty template rendering path unexercised. Acceptance: a Builder adds regression tests in server_test.go with an empty inventory asserting that GET /, GET /fragments/fleet, and GET /fragments/instance return HTTP 200, contain the expected empty-state text (\\\"No instances configured\\\", \\\"No instance selected\\\"), and do not produce template execution errors. Observed: templates have explicit branches for empty instances (fleet.html:36, instance.html:145), but grep shows no test in server_test.go exercises an empty App inventory. Required: HTTP handler regression tests for empty-inventory page and fragment rendering. Proposed test-work: add server tests verifying that GET /, /fragments/fleet, and /fragments/instance return 200 with empty-state messages when no instances are configured.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:19:02.012Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:06:06.276Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:06:06.276Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nCanopy supports a runtime with no configured or discovered instances, but its page and fragment routes are only tested with one configured instance. The empty operator surface can regress to a panic, 500, or broken template unnoticed.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\nWith `NewApp(Inventory{Instances: []}, ...)` and real templates:\\n\\n- `GET /` returns 200 and renders the fleet and selected-instance empty states.\\n- `GET /fragments/fleet` returns 200 and renders `No instances configured.`\\n- `GET /fragments/instance` returns 200 and renders `No instance selected` plus the instruction to add an instance.\\n- No route starts discovery, dereferences a missing selection, or requires host-specific Forest state.\\n\\nThis is test-only work; do not change empty-inventory behavior unless the scenario exposes a real defect.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nA table-driven HTTP test exercises all three routes with the actual embedded templates and an empty in-memory inventory, asserting status 200 and route-specific empty-state text. The focused server tests pass without systemd, Forest binaries, or network fixtures.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T18:58:32.84Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:19:02.012Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": false,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": true,\n      \"live\": true,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-tester-audit-divergence-stale\",\n    \"title\": \"Audit master commit divergence stale trust override lacks regression cover\",\n    \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nCanopy intentionally overrides a passing audit result to stale when the audited primary revision differs from the current primary revision. No observable test pins that trust signal.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\n- With `LastResult` pass/trusted and non-empty unequal `AuditedMaster` and `LastMaster`, the selected-instance audit badge uses the `stale` signal class.\\n- Preserve the reported pass/trusted text; stale describes revision applicability, not a rewritten audit result.\\n- Equal revisions, or a missing comparison revision, retain the result-derived class.\\n- Do not change audit classification policy in this job.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nExercise `GET /fragments/instance?instance=one` with real templates and a seeded successful snapshot. Table cases cover unequal, equal, and missing revision refs. Assert 200, the rendered audit badge class, and preserved result text. Avoid source-text assertions against `auditView` internals.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": \"c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a\",\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T18:58:47.383Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/iron-forest @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: canopy a101e023933a247460f9828b7cb8d3fce3a681ac\\nSurface: view.go:319 (auditView), templates/instance.html:40 (Audit trust metric card). Behaviors: when an instance's audited commit (AuditedMaster) differs from its current master commit (LastMaster) — indicating new commits have landed since the last audit — Canopy must classify the audit trust class as \\\"stale\\\" (signal class \\\"stale\\\") even if LastResult was \\\"pass\\\" or \\\"trusted\\\". Failing example: construct an AuditData with LastResult = \\\"pass\\\", LastMaster = \\\"sha-new\\\", and AuditedMaster = \\\"sha-old\\\", then invoke auditView or render instance.html; today no test in the repository exercises this divergence branch, leaving the critical \\\"is audited primary trustworthy?\\\" signal unpinned. Acceptance: a Builder adds a regression test proving that auditView produces TrustClass: \\\"stale\\\" when AuditedMaster and LastMaster are non-empty and unequal despite a passing LastResult, and that instance.html renders class=\\\"signal stale\\\" with the trust value. Observed: view.go:319 contains the explicit branch, but grep over all *_test.go files confirms AuditedMaster is never referenced in tests. Required: a regression test for the audit master divergence stale-override rule. Proposed test-work: add unit/template tests verifying that master revision divergence forces audit trust class to stale.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:23:56.147Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:29:01.259Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"done: c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:06:06.292Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:06:06.292Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nCanopy intentionally overrides a passing audit result to stale when the audited primary revision differs from the current primary revision. No observable test pins that trust signal.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\n- With `LastResult` pass/trusted and non-empty unequal `AuditedMaster` and `LastMaster`, the selected-instance audit badge uses the `stale` signal class.\\n- Preserve the reported pass/trusted text; stale describes revision applicability, not a rewritten audit result.\\n- Equal revisions, or a missing comparison revision, retain the result-derived class.\\n- Do not change audit classification policy in this job.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nExercise `GET /fragments/instance?instance=one` with real templates and a seeded successful snapshot. Table cases cover unequal, equal, and missing revision refs. Assert 200, the rendered audit badge class, and preserved result text. Avoid source-text assertions against `auditView` internals.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T18:58:42.895Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:29:01.259Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": true,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": false,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-tester-initial-collection-failure\",\n    \"title\": \"Initial instance collection failure unknown freshness and attempted state lack regression cover\",\n    \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nTests cover a collection failure only after a successful snapshot. They do not defend the stronger first-observation invariant: an instance that has never succeeded is unknown, never fresh or stale, while still showing the failed attempt.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\nAfter the first collection attempt fails for an instance with no prior snapshot:\\n\\n- Preserve no successful snapshot and zero `LastSuccess`.\\n- Record `LastAttempt` and the collector error.\\n- Render freshness as `unknown` and reachability as false.\\n- Render `LastObserved` as `attempted \\u003ctimestamp\\u003e`, surface the error, and keep the `Waiting for first observation` state.\\n- Do not start background discovery or depend on host state.\\n\\nThis is test-only work unless the scenario exposes a real defect.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nUse a deterministic failing collector for one `refreshOnce`, then exercise the real instance fragment/template. Assert HTTP 200, unknown/first-observation output, attempted timestamp, and visible failure; assert no fresh/stale classification. Existing success-then-failure retention coverage remains unchanged.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": {\n      \"agent\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n      \"principal\": \"none\",\n      \"until\": \"2026-09-04T23:33:53.108Z\"\n    },\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T18:59:00.096Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/iron-forest @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: canopy a101e023933a247460f9828b7cb8d3fce3a681ac\\nSurface: view.go:208-213 (instanceView), view.go:160 (classifyFreshness), templates/instance.html:18 (\\\"Waiting for first observation\\\"). Behaviors: when an instance has never completed a successful collection (e.g. host unreachable or binary failure on first launch), Canopy must maintain its freshness as \\\"unknown\\\" (never \\\"stale\\\" or \\\"fresh\\\"), set Reachable: false, record LastObserved with prefix \\\"attempted \\u003ctimestamp\\u003e\\\", surface the failure in Errors, and render the \\\"Waiting for first observation\\\" card. Failing example: configure an instance whose collector fails immediately on the first attempt without any prior successful snapshot; today TestRefreshRetainsLastSuccessfulSnapshotOnFailure in app_test.go only tests failure after an initial success (transitioning to \\\"stale\\\"), leaving the initial-failure path (view.go:210) untested. Acceptance: a Builder adds a regression test in app_test.go asserting that after an initial refresh failure, app.state(id) has Snapshot == nil, instanceView has Freshness: \\\"unknown\\\", Reachable: false, LastObserved prefixed with \\\"attempted \\\", Errors containing the collector error, and instance.html rendering the waiting-title card. Observed: view.go:210 sets \\\"attempted \\\" when Snapshot is nil and LastAttempt is non-zero, but grep shows \\\"attempted\\\" is never asserted in any test file. Required: a regression test in app_test.go for initial instance collection failure. Proposed test-work: add an app/view regression test proving an instance failing its initial collection reports unknown freshness, attempted timestamp, and the waiting card.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:26:41.534Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:29:23.983Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"ask: Implementation and checks are complete at f93e178 on forest/canopy-tester-initial-collection-failure/first-failure-proof; PR https://github.com/misty-step/canopy/pull/11. Focused regression, all Go tests, and go vet pass. This executive session has no Runner FOREST_RUN_ID, so it cannot publish authorized Builder review-request evidence. An authorized Builder Run must adopt this exact branch, validate/rebase if needed, and publish forest.review-request.v2 for tracker powder. Do not treat the PR or raw branch push as Gate approval or job completion.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:31:26.472Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"text\": \"answer: Executive recovery complete: PR #11 closed and remote forest branch deleted. No review-request evidence was created. Implementation is preserved in the local ref executive/initial-collection-failure-preserved at f93e178. A normal Builder may select this job, inspect/cherry-pick that commit into its own fresh forest branch if useful, rerun checks, and publish through the authorized Runner Gate. Do not treat prior PR or checks as approval.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:33:53.108Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:06:06.282Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:06:06.282Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nTests cover a collection failure only after a successful snapshot. They do not defend the stronger first-observation invariant: an instance that has never succeeded is unknown, never fresh or stale, while still showing the failed attempt.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\nAfter the first collection attempt fails for an instance with no prior snapshot:\\n\\n- Preserve no successful snapshot and zero `LastSuccess`.\\n- Record `LastAttempt` and the collector error.\\n- Render freshness as `unknown` and reachability as false.\\n- Render `LastObserved` as `attempted \\u003ctimestamp\\u003e`, surface the error, and keep the `Waiting for first observation` state.\\n- Do not start background discovery or depend on host state.\\n\\nThis is test-only work unless the scenario exposes a real defect.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nUse a deterministic failing collector for one `refreshOnce`, then exercise the real instance fragment/template. Assert HTTP 200, unknown/first-observation output, attempted timestamp, and visible failure; assert no fresh/stale classification. Existing success-then-failure retention coverage remains unchanged.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T18:58:54.638Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:33:53.108Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": false,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": true,\n      \"live\": true,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-tester-route-param-validation\",\n    \"title\": \"HTTP route instance parameter traversal and invalid identifier rejection lack regression cover\",\n    \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nHTTP instance parameters use the shared route-identifier validator before lookup or command execution, but tests cover only an unknown instance and one malformed run ID. The route boundary is not pinned across instance-accepting handlers.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\n- `/`, `/fragments/fleet`, and `/fragments/instance` allow a missing optional `instance`; `/logs` requires it.\\n- Present-empty or duplicate `instance` values return 400.\\n- Dot/traversal values, Unicode whitespace/control, `/` or `\\\\\\\\`, and the validator's unsafe punctuation classes return 400 before selection or collector execution.\\n- A syntactically valid unknown instance returns 404, not 400.\\n- Missing or malformed `run` on `/logs` returns 400 without calling `Collector.Logs`.\\n- A syntactically valid unknown run reaches the collector and retains the existing 200 unknown-log fragment behavior.\\n- Do not change accepted identifier policy.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nA table-driven handler test covers every instance-accepting route, parameter cardinality, and each malformed class at least once; every route gets a representative traversal/separator case. A recording collector proves invalid `/logs` requests make zero calls. Keep the existing valid-unknown run assertion. Focused server tests pass.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": {\n      \"agent\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n      \"principal\": \"none\",\n      \"until\": \"2026-09-04T23:28:55.422Z\"\n    },\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T18:59:11.267Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/iron-forest @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: canopy a101e023933a247460f9828b7cb8d3fce3a681ac\\nSurface: server.go:142 (instanceParam), server.go:171 (runParam), inventory.go:138 (validateRouteIdentifier), routes GET /, GET /fragments/fleet, GET /fragments/instance, GET /logs. Behaviors: query parameter values for instance must be validated before routing or execution: path traversal (\\\"..\\\", \\\".\\\"), route separators (\\\"/\\\", \\\"\\\\\\\"), control characters, and shell metacharacters must be rejected with HTTP 400 Bad Request across /, /fragments/fleet, /fragments/instance, and /logs. Failing example: invoke GET /?instance=.. or GET /fragments/instance?instance=bad%2Fid or GET /logs?instance=..\\u0026run=run-1; today server_test.go only tests run parameter rejection on /logs (TestHandlerRejectsUnknownAndMalformedRun), leaving instance parameter malformed/traversal validation unexercised on all routes. Acceptance: a Builder adds test cases in server_test.go asserting that requests with invalid instance parameters (e.g. instance=.., instance=bad/id, instance=bad;id) return HTTP 400 Bad Request across /, /fragments/fleet, /fragments/instance, and /logs. Observed: server.go:150 checks validateRouteIdentifier for instanceParam and returns errBadInstance (status 400), but server_test.go only asserts status 404 for unknown instance and tests no malformed instance parameter. Required: HTTP route regression tests for malformed and traversal instance parameters. Proposed test-work: add server regression tests asserting invalid and traversal instance query parameters return HTTP 400 across all routes.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:28:55.422Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:06:06.245Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:06:06.245Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nHTTP instance parameters use the shared route-identifier validator before lookup or command execution, but tests cover only an unknown instance and one malformed run ID. The route boundary is not pinned across instance-accepting handlers.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\n- `/`, `/fragments/fleet`, and `/fragments/instance` allow a missing optional `instance`; `/logs` requires it.\\n- Present-empty or duplicate `instance` values return 400.\\n- Dot/traversal values, Unicode whitespace/control, `/` or `\\\\\\\\`, and the validator's unsafe punctuation classes return 4